//
// WHY THIS EXISTS (holes it closes):
//   • Cookie is httpOnly + Secure + SameSite=Lax, signed via lib/session.ts.
//   • REDIRECT BASELINE: a RELATIVE `Location`, never new URL(path, req.url)
//     (req.url is the internal localhost:PORT bind -> dead page for real users).
//   • CROSS-SITE POSTs (login CSRF) get a plain 403 before any other work.
//   • GENERIC failures: login never says whether the email or the password was
//     wrong, and a missing user still pays one bcrypt compare (no timing oracle).
//   • THROTTLE: per-IP + per-email sliding window, in-process. WATCH-TRIGGER: this
//     Map lives in ONE process; when the site runs >1 instance, move it to a DB
//     table (attempts: key, at) or every instance gets its own budget.
//   • ?error=<code> only, mapped to fixed copy by authErrorMessage(): a page never
//     shows text from the URL.
//   • ROLES: users.role is 'user' | 'admin' (DB default 'user'). NOTHING here or in
//     the routes grants admin except redeemInvite() (an invite link the site owner
//     made in Zavi). NEVER grant a role by signup order, first user, email or env.
//     Gate every admin-only page / route handler / server action with
//     requireAdminPage() / requireAdminRoute() / requireAdminAction().
